            ],
            "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
            "notes": "Transaction integrity is enforced by ECDSA signatures. Any modification invalidates the signature."
          },
          "test_procedure": "1. Locate the ECDSA signature verification implementation in the execution client.\n2. Test signature verification with valid transactions to establish baseline behavior.\n3. Submit transactions with corrupted v, r, or s signature components and verify rejection.\n4. Test edge cases in ECDSA verification (e.g., signature malleability, zero values, boundary values).\n5. Verify that signature verification failures result in immediate transaction rejection without further processing.\n6. Check that error handling does not leak information about why signature verification failed.",
          "bug_class": "Cryptographic Validation",
          "risk_category": "Tampering",
